On Nov 10, 7:00 pm, Dasein <dasein2...@hotmail.com> wrote:
> I'm a beginner and yet to ascend, but my most fun games have been with
> challenging classes like Tourist and Healer.

I've had quite a bit of fun with Tourist myself.  It seems like a
pretty well-balanced role.  The major caveat is that it takes a LONG
time to get your strength up to where you can carry any decent amount
of inventory, so in the early game you find yourself leaving lots of
wands and potions and scrolls and any spellbooks you happen across
just laying around on the ground wherever they are because you can't
carry them.  Either that or you play what basically amounts to a
nudist conduct until you get gauntlets of power or DSM and a BOH.

Also, if you run out of darts too early you're in hot water.  The
first Tourist game I played, my starting darts were blessed, so by the
time they all evaporated (or whatever you call it when a projectile
cannot be recovered) I had acquired a unicorn horn.  This gave me an
unfortunate habit of using darts to kill non-threatening things like
lichens, just to build up my skill, a practice that I have had to
unlearn in subsequent games when my darts were not blessed.

But I like the balance with Tourist of being able, with practice, to
effectively handle both spells (identify is particularly handy) and
melee combat.  Most of the other roles I've tried thus far are pretty
lousy at one or the other.  (There are some roles I haven't tried yet,
including Healer.)


